<div class="field"><label>Restaurant type</label><select id="type"><option value="">All types</option></select></div>
<div class="field"><label>Minimum rating</label><select id="rating"><option value="0">Any rating</option><option value="2.5">2.5+</option><option value="3">3.0+</option><option value="3.5">3.5+</option><option value="4">4.0+</option><option value="4.5">4.5+</option></select></div>
<div class="field"><label>Maximum cost (for two)</label><select id="cost"><option value="999999">Any cost</option><option value="300">₹300</option><option value="500">₹500</option><option value="800">₹800</option><option value="1200">₹1,200</option><option value="2000">₹2,000</option></select></div>
<div class="field"><label>Online order</label><select id="online"><option value="">All</option><option>Yes</option><option>No</option></select></div>
<div class="field"><label>Table booking</label><select id="booking"><option value="">All</option><option>Yes</option><option>No</option></select></div>
<div class="filter-actions"><button class="btn secondary" id="reset">Reset</button><button class="btn primary" id="export">↓ Export CSV</button></div>
</section>
<div class="section-head"><h2>Executive overview</h2><span>Metrics update with your filters</span></div>
<section class="kpis">
<div class="kpi"><div class="label">Total restaurants</div><div class="value" id="kTotal">—</div><div class="hint">Matching current filters</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="label">Average rating</div><div class="value" id="kRating">—</div><div class="hint">Out of 5 · rated restaurants only</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="label">Average cost for two</div><div class="value" id="kCost">—</div><div class="hint">Indian rupees (₹)</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="label">Total votes</div><div class="value" id="kVotes">—</div><div class="hint">Sum of restaurant votes</div></div>
</section>
<section class="grid2">
<div class="panel"><h3>Rating distribution</h3><div class="sub">Number of restaurants in each rating band</div><div class="chart bars" id="ratingBars"></div></div>
<div class="panel"><h3>Online ordering preference</h3><div class="sub">Share of restaurants accepting online orders</div><div class="donut-wrap"><div class="donut" id="onlineDonut"><div class="donut-center" id="onlinePct">—<small>YES</small></div></div><div class="key" id="onlineKey"></div></div></div>
</section>
<section class="grid3">
<div class="panel"><h3>Restaurant types</h3><div class="sub">Restaurant count by listed type</div><div class="bars" id="typeBars"></div></div>
<div class="panel"><h3>Cost vs. rating</h3><div class="sub">Average rating grouped by cost band</div><div class="bars" id="costBars"></div></div>
<div class="panel"><h3>Table booking</h3><div class="sub">Restaurants offering table booking</div><div class="donut-wrap"><div class="donut" id="bookingDonut"><div class="donut-center" id="bookingPct">—<small>YES</small></div></div><div class="key" id="bookingKey"></div></div></div>
</section>
<section class="grid2">
<div class="panel"><h3>Top-rated restaurants</h3><div class="sub">Highest-rated restaurants in the filtered dataset</div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Restaurant</th><th>Type</th><th>Rating</th><th>Votes</th><th>Cost for two</th></tr></thead><tbody id="topRows"></tbody></table></div></div>
<div class="panel"><h3>Location & cuisine intelligence</h3><div class="sub">Data availability check</div><div class="disabled"><b>Location comparison unavailable</b><br>The uploaded CSV does not include a location or city column. Add a location field to enable geographic distribution and comparisons.</div><div style="height:10px"></div><div class="disabled"><b>Cuisine comparison unavailable</b><br>The file includes <i>listed_in(type)</i> (Dining, Cafes, Buffet, other), but no cuisine column. Restaurant type is used as the available category instead.</div></div>
</section>
<section class="panel" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="table-top"><div><h3>Restaurant detail</h3><div class="sub" style="margin:3px 0 0">All rows matching the active filters · export to CSV for further analysis</div></div><span class="pill" id="tableCount">0 rows</span></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Restaurant</th><th>Type</th><th>Rating</th><th>Votes</th><th>Cost for two</th><th>Online order</th><th>Table booking</th></tr></thead><tbody id="allRows"></tbody></table></div></section>
<div class="section-head"><h2>Data notes</h2></div><div class="note">Source: uploaded <b>zomato.csv</b> (148 restaurant records). Average rating excludes records without a parseable rating. The source contains restaurant name, online order, table booking, rating, votes, approximate cost for two and listed restaurant type. No cuisine or location fields are present. Cost values are displayed as supplied; currency is assumed to be INR based on the dataset context.</div>
<footer>Restaurant Analytics Dashboard · Built from your uploaded CSV · Filters and CSV export run in your browser</footer>
